Description: palOS first-boot setup
 What a new palOS computer shows the first time it starts after installing:
 a short welcome film (shown once), joining Wi-Fi, then either creating the
 first account (name, picture, password, light or dark look) or restoring
 from a Time Turner backup on a drive or network share: accounts with their
 passwords, home folders, Wi-Fi networks and apps (snaps too) come back, and Time Turner
 carries on backing up. When it's done the computer goes to the normal palOS
 login screen.
 .
 If the setup screen can't run on a computer, palOS tries it again without the
 graphics card, then offers Basic Setup, which only creates the first account.
 .
 The installer turns it on for the new system; sudo palos-firstboot-rerun
 turns it on again.
